e same set of\nSchur functions appear with nonzero coeﬃcient. In other words, we consider the question\nof when two skew diagrams have equal Schur support (Deﬁnition 1). This question has\nreceived less attention, with the most substantial progress coming from McNamara in\n2007 [6] and from McNamara and van Willigenburg in 2011 [7].\nthe electronic journal of combinatorics 26(3) (2019), #P3.52\n1--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEquality of Schur (https://www-users.cse.umn.edu/~reiner/REU/REU2017notes/problem-1-presentation.pdf)\nciteturn2search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.0 years ago; Ribbons ... α has full equivalence class, then N < Pm α −(m −j −2) for ... Conjecture\nThe above necessary condition is sufficient for a ribbon to have full\n| Necessary Condition for Full E.C\n--- | ---\nEquality of Schur\nSupports of\nRibbons\nGaetz, Hardt,\nSridhar, Tran\nPreliminaries\nMain Results\nOther Results\nAcknowledgements\nReferences  | Theorem (S, G, H, Tran, ’17)\nLet α = (α 1, α 2, . . . , α m) be a ribbon, where α ≥α ≥· · · ≥α m. If\n1 2\nα has full equivalence class, then N < Pm α −(m −j −2) for\nj i=j+1 i\nall j ≤m −2, where\nN = max{k| X (k −α i) ≤m −j −2}.\nj\ni≤j: αi<k\nWe prove the contrapositive by assuming\nm\nN ≥ X α −(m −j −2)\nj i\ni=j+1\nand showing that there exists a content for an LR-filling of α\n(j j+1)\nthat is not the content of any LR-filling of α.\nConjecture\nThe above necessary condition is sufficient for a ribbon to have full\nequivalence class.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSupportEqualitiesAmongRibbonSchurFunctions (https://web.math.princeton.edu/~ssridhar/research/posters/SchurPoster.pdf)\nciteturn2search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; We conjecture that our necessary condition is also sufﬁcient. ... A ribbon α = (α1, α2, . . . , αm) is said to have full equivalence class if ... Question: Which connected ribbons have full equ